### Why Morningstar believes it is severely undervalued

Morningstar’s fair value of $270 corresponds to a valuation of approximately:
- Based on 2026 Adjusted EPS: ~32x PE
- Morningstar expects organic revenue to grow at a compound annual rate of 7% (to 2028) and adjusted EPS to grow at a compound annual rate of approximately 13%

The core logic of Morning Star is:
1. Current prices reflect "trough" performance from post-pandemic destocking, but bioprocess recovery has begun
2. Danaher’s business model quality (75% recurring revenue, high switching costs) warrants premium valuation
3. Benefit from the long-term trend of increasing biopharmaceutical penetration and new therapies (CGT)

### Compare to historical valuations

Danaher's historical five-year average price-to-earnings ratio is about 30-35x (adjusted), and the current adjusted PE ratio of about 21x is at the lower edge of the historical valuation range.

